# Living Terrain — World Canon

Philosophy is complete. Implementation expresses this world; it does not redefine it.

## The four rooms

| Room | Route | What it holds |
|---|---|---|
| **The Constellation** | `/` | Living relational truth — how everything connects |
| **The Atlas** | `/atlas` | Relationships among Territories, Threads, Artifacts, and Investigations — including charted **maps** (what remains after the survey) |
| **The Shelves** | `/inquiry` | Ongoing inquiry — essays, field notes, shorter writing |
| **The Observatory** | `/observatory` | Investigations still forming |

## Atlas 2.0 types (Phase 0–1 frozen; Phase 2 complete)

Canonical internal architecture. Full tables: `docs/atlas-2.0-phase-0.md`. Typed layer: `lib/atlas/model.ts`. Do not begin Phase 3 without approval.

| Type | Meaning | Canonical source |
|---|---|---|
| **Territory** | A region/domain of the terrain | Five Root Territories (`lib/atlas/architecture.ts`) |
| **Thread** | A recurring pattern followed across territories | Ten essay/content Threads only (`lib/threads/vocabulary.ts`, `/threads/*`) |
| **Artifact** | Concrete work / evidence | Maps, chambers, essays, plates, quotations, field notes |
| **Investigation** | Active question / inquiry | Void questions, Observatory, Shelves inquiry |

**Territory ≠ Thread:** Do not infer that every Territory or major-concept requires a Thread.

**Disambiguation (required):** Thread = essay/content Thread only. **Trail** = Atlas visitor/session path. **Strand** = former `ConnectionKind: "thread"`. **Pathway** = Observatory pathway only. Do not invent unsupported relationships.

**Phase 1 freeze:** V1 Territory-only = `body`, `adaptation`, `time`, `meaning`, `reality`. Both = `relationship`, `feedback`, `technology`, `constraint`, `participation`. Aliases = `th-relationship` → Thread `relationship`, `th-consciousness` → Thread `consciousness` (semantic only; `/themes/*` URLs unchanged in Phase 2). All other listed major-concepts remain distinct; no retirements.

